 "originality_note": "Composed from scratch for this film: the call/answer mukhda, its rhythm (lilting quarter-eighth cells landing on the anticipated last eighth of beat 3), the harmony and every countermelody are original. No existing film or wedding song is used, quoted or paraphrased; the raga colours (Khamaj komal ni, Charukeshi komal dha, Bhupali pentatonic) are shared idioms, not borrowed melodies.",
 "revision_note": "Revised after a three-judge review and independent technical and musical checks. Curtains: strings release at 28.25, a subito-pp hush with piano and bass silent, then a crescendo; the tihai grows into sam at 30.0. Melody: a dotted launch in bar 9, murkis before the mukhda leaps and on Pa at 30.75, the bride blooms to B5 at 17.0, the card carries the call at half speed with a meend and kans, and the violin reaches tar Sa on the signature at 55.0. Texture: real santoor rolls on same-pitch tremolos, sparse santoor drops under the bride and the card, sitar answers in bars 2 and 4, fewer bells, and a bar-18 tihai that lands accented on the final chord."
}
